      "message": "This was actually a clean cherry-pick, and the commit is now in Linus\u0027 tree, so the appropriate tag would be \"UPSTREAM:\".  The \"BACKPORT:\" tag is appropriate for earlier kernels where it doesn\u0027t cherry-pick cleanly.  \"FROMGIT:\" is only for cherry-picking from a maintainer\u0027s tree, not Linus\u0027 tree (though I\u0027ve been told that the Android team actually wants \"FROMLIST:\" for that case, which differs from Chrome OS convention).",
